      "writtenOn": "2026-09-16T05:27:45Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This is motivated by the same concern as `pruneOnStartup` flag. Today, depending on the combination of `startTime` and when Gerrit happens to be restarted, the first periodic run can fire almost immediately after boot. For a heavy job like cache pruning that\u0027s undesirable as right after a restart the server is warming caches and handling reconnecting clients, and we\u0027d rather not add background I/O contention during that window. This change tries to address this gap and make things easier and deterministic for the admins.",
      "parentUuid": "6d482444_20f11e5b",
      "revId": "4d9df897e1feb765506eaa778e67e7561f77402c",
      "serverId": "173816e5-2b9a-37c3-8a2e-48639d4f1153"
